{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" macro — no hand-written "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" classes, database actors, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation"},{"title":"How-to Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"]}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" turns persistence into a declare-and-register concern. You annotate a domain entity with "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; the macro generates its SwiftData ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" “shadow” class, the value↔model converters, and the "},{"code":"PersistableEntity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. A generic "},{"code":"EntityDB","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" actor and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceCoordinator"},{"type":"text","text":" build the container, synthesize one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" per registered "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and reuse the core "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" for debounced, batched writes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your reducers mutate plain value-type entities inside an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"; the plugin observes the changelog and writes through to SwiftData after a debounce. Reads happen once, at launch, into memory — the in-memory "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is the source of truth."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For low-level manual wiring (writing your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". For the macro details, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". To add cross-device iCloud sync on top, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Before-you-start","text":"Before you start","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide assumes a Swidux app already exists — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppReducer"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppStore"},{"type":"text","text":" are wired and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If not, follow "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a local-only persistence layer. It needs ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"no iCloud, CloudKit, or Push entitlements","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — only the sandbox ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.apple.security.network.client","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entitlement if your app also makes network calls (killswitch, analytics, feature flags). Adding sync entitlements to a local-only app is dead configuration and an App Review risk.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" product to your app target in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxPersistence\",","    ]",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Step-2-Annotate-your-domain-entity-with-Persisted","text":"Step 2: Annotate your domain entity with `@Persisted`","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A persisted entity is a value type that already satisfies "},{"code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"ID == UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" contract). Add "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","    var createdAt: Date","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This generates a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CardModel: @Model"},{"type":"text","text":" class with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"toDomain()"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"update(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":", plus "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"extension Card: PersistableEntity { typealias Model = CardModel }"},{"type":"text","text":". By default every stored property is mirrored directly onto the model — SwiftData persists scalars "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" composites natively, so no manual blob columns are needed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The generated model is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"CloudKit-safe by construction","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"same","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" model backs both the local and the synced container (see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","isActive":true},{"text":"). SwiftData’s CloudKit mirroring requires every non-optional attribute to be optional or carry a default value, and every relationship to be optional — validated when the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ModelContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is created. ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" satisfies this automatically:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-optional mirrored attributes get a default."}]},{"type":"text","text":" If you wrote one on the domain property ("},{"code":"var count: Int = 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), it is propagated verbatim; otherwise the macro fills a canonical default for the known SwiftData primitives ("},{"code":"String → \"\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Bool → false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", integers\/floats "},{"code":"→ 0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Date → .distantPast","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Data → Data()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"UUID → UUID()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). Defaults are inert locally — "},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" overwrites them on every load."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-primitive, non-optional properties"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (a custom "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" type, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URL"},{"type":"text","text":", an enum) have no default the macro can invent. Give the property a default ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"= …"},{"type":"text","text":"), make it optional, or mark it "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"type":"text","text":" — otherwise "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" emits a compile-time error."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Relationships are generated optional"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"var tags: [TagModel]? = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); a non-optional to-one ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Relation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a compile-time error (CloudKit forbids non-optional relationships).","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"text":" blob columns","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" default to "},{"code":"Data()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" type is CloudKit-safe through "},{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lives on the ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"entity"}]},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lives on ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state containers"}]},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" slices). They are different layers and never apply to the same type.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Marker macros for non-trivial properties","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Marker-macros-for-non-trivial-properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro can’t infer relationships, foreign keys, or which fields are derived. Four property markers (named to avoid SwiftData’s own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relationship"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Transient"},{"text":") tell ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" what to do:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","","    @Inline var styling: TextStyling                 \/\/ one opaque JSON Data column","    @ForeignKey var deckID: UUID                      \/\/ scalar parent reference","    @Relation(deleteRule: .cascade, inverse: \\TagModel.card)","    var tags: [Tag]                                   \/\/ SwiftData relationship","    @Ignored var renderedPreview: String?             \/\/ derived; omitted from the model","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Marker","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Effect","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"(none)"}]}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mirror the property directly (SwiftData persists scalars and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" composites).","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Force a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" value into a single JSON "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"text":" column (keeps a CloudKit record compact; sidesteps SwiftData ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-attribute edge cases).","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@ForeignKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intent marker on a "},{"code":"UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; functionally a mirrored scalar column."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relation(deleteRule:inverse:)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A SwiftData relationship to another "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" entity. The property’s type references the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain"}]},{"type":"text","text":" type ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Tag]"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tag?"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tag"},{"type":"text","text":"); the model substitutes the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"…Model"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inverse"},{"type":"text","text":" is a key path on the generated model, e.g. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\TagModel.card"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deleteRule"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxDeleteRule"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cascade"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".nullify"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".noAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".deny"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Ignored","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exclude a derived\/denormalized property. Must be optional so it can be reconstructed as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" on load."}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" does not generate an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Attribute(.unique)"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" — CloudKit forbids unique constraints. Identity is enforced by upsert-by-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" inside "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EntityDB"},{"type":"text","text":", so the same generated model works for both local and synced containers."}]}],"name":"Note"},{"level":2,"text":"Step 3: Put the `EntityStore` on your state","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-3-Put-the-EntityStore-on-your-state"},{"code":["@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    var cards: EntityStore<Card> = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Your reducers mutate ","type":"text"},{"code":"state.cards","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" like any ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"state.cards[card.id] = card","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state.cards.modify(id) { … }"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"state.cards[id] = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every change is recorded for the plugin to drain.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 4: Build the coordinator and register the plugin","anchor":"Step-4-Build-the-coordinator-and-register-the-plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", build a local container, create a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", register its plugin, and run first-load hydration before constructing the store:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","extension Store where State == AppState, Action == AppAction {","    static func configured() async -> AppStore {","        let container = try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","","        let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","            entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","            container: container,","            debounce: .milliseconds(250)","        )","","        let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","        \/\/ Register UndoPlugin first if you use it — snapshots must precede writes.","        plugins.register(persistence.corePlugin)","","        var initial = AppState()","        await persistence.hydrate(into: &initial)   \/\/ first-load: fill EntityStores from disk","","        return Store(initialState: initial, reducer: { … }, plugins: plugins)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"hydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first-load only"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — it replaces each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" with the on-disk rows before any live edits exist. The only refresh path after launch is ","type":"text"},{"code":"rehydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which always ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"merges"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (preferring in-memory values) so a “refresh from disk” can never clobber unflushed writes or in-progress UI edits.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 5: Flush on background","anchor":"Step-5-Flush-on-background"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Writes are debounced, so drain them when the app is backgrounded or terminates:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .background {","        Task { await persistence.corePlugin.flush() }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Multiple entities and ordering","anchor":"Multiple-entities-and-ordering"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Register one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".entity(\\.keyPath)"},{"type":"text","text":" per "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.decks), .entity(\\.cards), .entity(\\.tags)],","    container: try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(","        models: [DeckModel.self, CardModel.self, TagModel.self]","    )",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass every generated "},{"code":"…Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" type to the container’s "},{"code":"models:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Writers flush in registration order — if entity B holds a "},{"code":"@Relation","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to A, register A’s entity first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Testing","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Testing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The whole stack runs against an in-memory SwiftData store, so persistence is unit-testable with no disk and no CloudKit:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let container = try ContainerFactory.makeInMemoryContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","let db = EntityDB(modelContainer: container)","","try await db.upsert(Card(id: id, quote: \"hi\", createdAt: .now), as: CardModel.self)","let all = try await db.fetchAll(CardModel.self)","#expect(all.first?.quote == \"hi\")"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To prove the rule-#8 merge guarantee, seed the store, make a live in-memory edit, call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coordinator.rehydrate(into:)"},{"text":", and assert the live edit survives.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Add Persistence","role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"abstract":[{"text":"Install the bundled ","type":"text"},{"code":"swidux-ref","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"abstract":[{"text":"Reference for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","title":"Macros","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","abstract":[{"text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Add a Parental Gate"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"EntityStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify.","type":"text"}],"title":"Add Analytics","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"abstract":[{"text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","title":"Getting Started with Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","abstract":[{"text":"Coalescing persistence plugin.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","title":"Building a Domain Plugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPaywall"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}],"role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","kind":"article","title":"Add a Paywall"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","title":"Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"EntityStore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"type":"topic","role":"article","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-